{
  "description": "Shared test vectors of the canonical payload hash, which the repository, the release builder and the platform compute the same way.",
  "format": {
    "payload": "The payload as the platform exports it inside a scenario (the injector contract's injector_contract_payload).",
    "attack_patterns": "The external IDs (attack_pattern_external_id) of the techniques the payload's contract holds (injector_contract_attack_patterns), in the order given.",
    "files": "The SHA-256 of each attached document's bytes, by document ID.",
    "canonical": "The canonical JSON text (RFC 8785), in UTF-8.",
    "sha256": "The SHA-256 of the canonical text: the payload's hash.",
    "refused": "The JSON pointer of the field this repository's canonical form refuses to hash without guessing: in the payload, or in its contract for a technique (/injector_contract_attack_patterns). A refusal is a limit of the repository's form, never a claim that the platform cannot hash the payload."
  },
  "rules": [
    "The canonical form keeps the payload's fields under their exported names, as each type defines them; a field of another type, a field the form does not know or a value of an unexpected type is refused.",
    "Left out by name, at their level only: payload_id, payload_external_id, payload_source, payload_status, payload_collector_type, payload_author_user, payload_author_team, payload_author_organization, payload_tags, payload_created_at, payload_updated_at, listened; in an output parser output_parser_id and its dates; in an output element contract_output_element_id, contract_output_element_tags and its dates; in a regex group regex_group_id and its dates.",
    "A field whose value is null, an empty string, an empty list or an empty object is left out, at every depth, and so is an object in a list whose fields are all left out; false and 0 are kept. An item of a list of texts that is null or empty is refused, never dropped.",
    "Sets, sorted and holding no item twice: payload_platforms, payload_expectations, each list of payload_expected_security_platforms, payload_output_parsers, their output_parser_contract_output_elements and contract_output_element_regex_groups, and the techniques. Texts sort by their UTF-16 code units; objects by their canonical text, compared in UTF-16 code units.",
    "Ordered lists keep their order and may repeat an item: payload_arguments, payload_prerequisites, ai_attack_converters.",
    "An attached file (executable_file, file_drop_file, the default_value of a document argument) enters by the SHA-256 of its bytes, in lower-case hexadecimal; its name does not enter.",
    "The techniques enter as payload_attack_patterns.",
    "Refused: a detection remediation (the export names its security platform by an identifier) and a free-form AI object (ai_attack_multi_turn, ai_attack_success_detector), when not empty.",
    "Numbers are integers within the safe range of RFC 8785 (2^53 - 1)."
  ],
